SUMMARY:Prime Minister w/Q&A | Additional Films and Guests
DESCRIPTION:This gripping documentary chronicles Jacinda Ardern navigatin
 g unprecedented national tragedies\, a volcanic eruption\, and a global p
 andemic as New Zealand's youngest female leader. By balancing immense pol
 itical pressure with first-time motherhood\, she redefines global leaders
 hip through an empathetic yet resolute approach. Packed with raw audio di
 aries and candid footage\, this film delivers a powerful\, inspiring port
 rait of a woman who proved that vulnerability and unyielding strength can
  rewrite the rules of power. [101 min\; documentary\; English]A Q&amp\;A 
 will follow the screening.  Co-sponsored by the Center of Excellence for 
 Women &amp\; Technology and the Office of the Vice Provost for Faculty an
 d Academic Affairs.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  This gripping documentary chronicles Ja
 cinda Ardern navigating unprecedented national tragedies\, a volcanic eru
 ption\, and a global pandemic as New Zealand's youngest female leader. By
  balancing immense political pressure with first-time motherhood\, she re
 defines global leadership through an empathetic yet resolute approach. Pa
 cked with raw audio diaries and candid footage\, this film delivers a pow
 erful\, inspiring portrait of a woman who proved that vulnerability and u
 nyielding strength can rewrite the rules of power. [101 min\; documentary
 \; English]</p><p><i><strong>A Q&amp\;A will follow the screening.</stron
 g></i></p><p>  Co-sponsored by the Center of Excellence for Women &amp\; 
 Technology and the Office of the Vice Provost for Faculty and Academic Af
 fairs.</p>
