SUMMARY:Postmodern Panic: Meta Horror Double Feature with Scream + Cabin 
 in the Woods | Friday Night Frights
DESCRIPTION:A double feature of two classics of meta-horror that never fo
 rget their slasher roots. 30th and 15th anniversary screenings.          
 Snacks\, drinks in resealable/enclosed containers (there are no cupholder
 s in the Cinema!)\, and finger foods that do not emit a strong odor or ma
 ke a mess are allowed for this double feature. Alcohol\, cigarettes\, ele
 ctronic cigarettes\, and illicit drugs are prohibited at IU Cinema.      
   Scream(Wes Craven\, USA\, 1996): The horror blockbuster that jumpstarte
 d a franchise that is still going strong\, Scream follows a series of mys
 terious deaths in a small town as an offbeat group of friends become the 
 target of a masked killer. As the body count rises\, the kids must learn 
 "the rules" of horror films to survive. [111 min\; horror\; English]     
    Cabin in the Woods(Drew Goddard\, USA\, 2011): When five college frien
 ds arrive at a remote forest vacation cabin\, little do they expect the h
 orrors that await them. One by one\, they fall victim to backwoods zombie
 s\, soon discovering that there is more going on than meets the eye. [95 
 min\; horror\; English]
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<div class="collapsed individual-film__intro
  collapsed bg-none section" id="content"><div class="row"><div class="lay
 out"><div class="text"><p class="text screening-highlight"><strong>A doub
 le feature of two classics of meta-horror that never forget their slasher
  roots. 30th and 15th anniversary screenings.</strong></p><p>          Sn
 acks\, drinks in resealable/enclosed containers (there are no cupholders 
 in the Cinema!)\, and finger foods that do not emit a strong odor or make
  a mess are allowed for this double feature. Alcohol\, cigarettes\, elect
 ronic cigarettes\, and illicit drugs are prohibited at IU Cinema.        
 </p></div></div></div></div><div class="section bg-none individual-film__
 intro"><div class="row"><div class="layout"><div class="text"><p><i><stro
 ng>Scream</strong></i><strong>(Wes Craven\, USA\, 1996):</strong> The hor
 ror blockbuster that jumpstarted a franchise that is still going strong\,
  <i>Scream</i> follows a series of mysterious deaths in a small town as a
 n offbeat group of friends become the target of a masked killer. As the b
 ody count rises\, the kids must learn "the rules" of horror films to surv
 ive. [111 min\; horror\; English]        </p><p><i><strong>Cabin in the W
 oods</strong></i><strong>(Drew Goddard\, USA\, 2011):</strong> When five 
 college friends arrive at a remote forest vacation cabin\, little do they
  expect the horrors that await them. One by one\, they fall victim to bac
 kwoods zombies\, soon discovering that there is more going on than meets 
 the eye. [95 min\; horror\; English]        </p></div></div></div></div>
