SUMMARY:Manhunter: The Final Cut | Additional Films and Guests
DESCRIPTION:A retired criminal profiler (William Petersen) reluctantly re
 turns to the FBI to help track down a serial killer of families and is fo
 rced to consult an expert: the imprisoned Dr. Hannibal Lecktor (Brian Cox
  in a subtly chilling performance). The third feature written and directe
 d by Michael Mann is a gripping adaptation of the first of Thomas Harris'
  four novels featuring the iconic murderer Lecter (whose spelling was cha
 nged for Mann's film)\, and benefits from the filmmaker's typically strik
 ing visuals as well as a top-notch supporting cast\, including Tom Noonan
  as the hunted killer and three-time Oscar nominee Joan Allen as his blin
 d love interest. This new 4K cut\, overseen by Mann\, enhances the film's
  depth\, visual clarity and sound\, offering audiences the ultimate immer
 sive version that is both a restoration and a final edit. This 4K scan of
  the original 35mm negative—with a few shots from an interpositive—wa
 s conformed and digitally restored at L'Immagine Ritrovata in Bologna\, s
 trictly following the new reference edit done by Michael Mann. [122 min\;
  mystery\, thriller\; English]
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  A retired criminal profiler (William Pe
 tersen) reluctantly returns to the FBI to help track down a serial killer
  of families and is forced to consult an expert: the imprisoned Dr. Hanni
 bal Lecktor (Brian Cox in a subtly chilling performance). The third featu
 re written and directed by Michael Mann is a gripping adaptation of the f
 irst of Thomas Harris' four novels featuring the iconic murderer Lecter (
 whose spelling was changed for Mann's film)\, and benefits from the filmm
 aker's typically striking visuals as well as a top-notch supporting cast\
 , including Tom Noonan as the hunted killer and three-time Oscar nominee 
 Joan Allen as his blind love interest. This new 4K cut\, overseen by Mann
 \, enhances the film's depth\, visual clarity and sound\, offering audien
 ces the ultimate immersive version that is both a restoration and a final
  edit. This 4K scan of the original 35mm negative—with a few shots from
  an interpositive—was conformed and digitally restored at L'Immagine Ri
 trovata in Bologna\, strictly following the new reference edit done by Mi
 chael Mann. [122 min\; mystery\, thriller\; English]</p>
